IMPORT prelude

-- A New Tax System (Australian Business Number) Act 1999 (Commonwealth) -- am I entitled to an ABN, how do I get one, what
-- must I tell the Registrar, and when can it be taken away?
--
-- SEAT: the person carrying on an enterprise -- the platform rider who wants an ABN; the founder whose new company needs
-- one. Every decision is phrased as that person asks it, from facts they could state. Where the Act speaks to the Registrar
-- (ss 10, 11, 13, 15, 18, 19), the encoding says what it means for that person: the Registrar must register them, may cancel
-- them, must tell them, must give them at least 14 days.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 5A (religious practitioners); s 8 (entitlement to an ABN); s 9 (applying; the TFN not compelled);
-- s 10 (when the Registrar must register you); s 11(2) (date of effect may be backdated); s 13(2)-(4) (treating a 28-day
-- silence as a refusal); s 14 (notifying changes within 28 days); s 15 (information on request; at least 14 days); s 16(1),
-- (2) (who carries the duty for a partnership or unincorporated association); s 18(1)-(6) (cancellation, reasons and its
-- date of effect); s 19 (reinstatement); s 21 (reviewable ABN decisions); s 23(1) (identification offence); s 41 ("business",
-- "carrying on", "enterprise", "Corporations Act company"). Through s 41, the meaning of "enterprise" in s 9-20 of the
-- A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 is worked out from facts (a departure from the defaults: see NOTES.md).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 32, compilation date 30 June 2026 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 57, 2026"; register id
-- C2026C00290), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00467.txt (retrieved 2026-10-13).
-- Also used: A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999, Compilation No. 96, compilation date 1 January 2026
-- ("Includes amendments: Act No. 72, 2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../../a-new-tax-system-goods-and-services-tax-act-1999/registers/source-bundle/C2004A00446.txt: s 9-20 (enterprise)
-- only. No regulations set a number this encoding needs.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: application of the Act to government entities, super funds and RSE licensees (s 5); representatives (ss 9A,
-- 10A, 11A, 18(1A)); the Registrar changing your ABN (s 17); the register, its entries and public access (ss 24-27, 29A);
-- confidentiality (s 30); the offences about associates and representatives (s 23(2), (3)); the defences in s 16(3) and the
-- penalty under s 8C of the Taxation Administration Act 1953 for breaching ss 14-15 (in another Act); the objection
-- procedure itself (Part IVC of that Act); machinery (ss 1-4, 6, 7, 24, 28, 29, 31-36). Borrowed terms are asked as facts:
-- employee, withholding payment, "connected with the indirect tax zone", "limited registration entity", partnership,
-- associate, approved form, charity and the other s 9-20(1)(d)-(h) bodies.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use as advice.
-- Judgments the Act hands to the Registrar are INPUTS ("if the Registrar is satisfied that ...").

§ `A New Tax System (Australian Business Number) Act 1999`

§§ `s 41 and GST Act s 9-20 -- is what I do an enterprise`

-- s 41: "enterprise has the meaning given by section 9-20 of the A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999."
-- GST Act s 9-20(1): "An enterprise is an activity, or series of activities, done: (a) in the form of a *business; or (b) in
-- the form of an adventure or concern in the nature of trade; or (c) on a regular or continuous basis, in the form of a
-- lease, licence or other grant of an interest in property; or (d) by the trustee of a fund ... to which deductible gifts
-- can be made; or (da) by a trustee of a *complying superannuation fund ...; or (e) by a charity; or (g) by the
-- Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, or by a body corporate ... established for a public purpose ...; or (h) by a trustee
-- of a fund covered by item 2 of the table in section 30-15 of the ITAA 1997 ..."
-- s 41: "business includes any profession, trade, employment, vocation or calling, but does not include occupation as an
-- employee."
-- Plain gloss: an enterprise is a business, a one-off trading venture, regular letting of property, or the activity of
-- certain public and charitable bodies.
DECLARE `Form of my activity` IS ONE OF
    `a business: a profession, trade, vocation or calling`
    `an adventure or concern in the nature of trade`
    `a regular or continuous lease, licence or other grant of an interest in property`
    `done by a charity, a deductible gift or complying superannuation fund trustee, or a government body`
    `none of these`

-- The s 9-20(2)(c) limb turns on the kind of entity; "entity" is GST Act s 184-1, borrowed and asked.
DECLARE `Kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a partnership all or most of whose members are individuals`
    `a company`
    `another entity`

DECLARE `What I do` HAS
    `its form` IS A `Form of my activity`
    @desc Which form in GST Act s 9-20(1) the activity takes, if any
    `I do it as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you do it as someone's employee
    `I do it to earn payments to a director, office holder or labour-hire worker` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you do it to earn a withholding payment covered by GST Act s 9-20(4) other than as an employee: a payment to a company director, an office holder, or under a labour hire arrangement
    `I supply services as an office holder in an office accepted in the course of an enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you supply the services as the holder of an office you accepted in the course of, or in connection with, an enterprise (the exception in s 9-20(2)(a))
    `it is a private recreational pursuit or hobby` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it is a private recreational pursuit or hobby
    `I have a reasonable expectation of profit or gain` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you have a reasonable expectation of profit or gain from it
    `I do it as a member of a local governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you do it as a member of a local council or other local governing body
    `I am a religious practitioner doing it in my vocation as a member of a religious institution, not as its employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether s 5A moves the activity to your religious institution

-- GST Act s 9-20(2): "However, enterprise does not include an activity, or series of activities, done: (a) by a person as an
-- employee or in connection with earning *withholding payments covered by subsection (4) (unless the activity or series is
-- done in supplying services as the holder of an office that the person has accepted in the course of or in connection with
-- an activity or series of activities of a kind mentioned in subsection (1)); or (b) as a private recreational pursuit or
-- hobby; or (c) by an individual (other than a trustee of a charitable fund, ...), or a *partnership (all or most of the
-- members of which are individuals), without a reasonable expectation of profit or gain; or (d) as a member of a local
-- governing body ..."
-- The exception in (a) is read as rescuing only the withholding-payment limb, since an office holder is not an employee
-- (an inference). The charitable-trustee carve-out from (c) falls under `another entity`.
@export Does an exclusion take what I do out of being an enterprise (GST Act s 9-20(2))?
GIVEN `the activity` IS A `What I do` @desc What you do and how
      `I am` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What kind of entity you are
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I do excluded from being an enterprise` IF
        `the activity`'s `I do it as an employee`
    OR  (    `the activity`'s `I do it to earn payments to a director, office holder or labour-hire worker`
         AND (NOT `the activity`'s `I supply services as an office holder in an office accepted in the course of an enterprise`))
    OR  `the activity`'s `it is a private recreational pursuit or hobby`
    OR  (    (NOT `the activity`'s `I have a reasonable expectation of profit or gain`)
         AND (CONSIDER `I am`
              WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
              WHEN `a partnership all or most of whose members are individuals` THEN TRUE
              OTHERWISE FALSE))
    OR  `the activity`'s `I do it as a member of a local governing body`

@export Is what I do an enterprise (ABN Act s 41, GST Act s 9-20)?
GIVEN `the activity` IS A `What I do` @desc What you do and how
      `I am` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What kind of entity you are
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I do an enterprise` IF
        (NOT (`the activity`'s `its form` EQUALS `none of these`))
    AND (NOT `Is what I do excluded from being an enterprise` `the activity` `I am`)

§§ `s 5A -- is it mine or my religious institution's`

-- s 5A: "If a *religious practitioner: (a) does an activity ... (i) in pursuit of his or her vocation as a religious
-- practitioner; and (ii) as a member of a religious institution; and (b) does not do the activity ... as an employee or
-- agent of the religious institution or another entity; this Act applies as if the activity ... had been done by the
-- religious institution and not by the religious practitioner."
@export Is the activity treated as my religious institution's rather than mine (s 5A)?
GIVEN `the activity` IS A `What I do` @desc What you do and how
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it my religious institution's activity, not mine` IF
    `the activity`'s `I am a religious practitioner doing it in my vocation as a member of a religious institution, not as its employee or agent`

§§ `s 8 -- am I entitled to an ABN`

-- s 8(1): "*You are entitled to have an Australian Business Number (*ABN) if: (a) you are *carrying on an *enterprise in
-- *Australia; or (b) in the course or furtherance of carrying on an enterprise, you make *supplies that are *connected with
-- the indirect tax zone."
-- (2): "A *Corporations Act company is entitled to have an Australian Business Number (*ABN)."
-- (3): "However, a limited registration entity (within the meaning of the A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act
-- 1999) is not entitled to an *ABN."
-- s 41: "carrying on an *enterprise includes doing anything in the course of the commencement or termination of the
-- enterprise." "Corporations Act company means a body registered as a company under the Corporations Act 2001."
DECLARE `Me and my enterprise` HAS
    `I am` IS A `Kind of entity`
    @desc What kind of entity you are
    `I am a company registered under the Corporations Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are a body registered as a company under the Corporations Act 2001 (for example a Pty Ltd registered with ASIC)
    `I am a limited registration entity under the GST Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are a limited registration entity within the meaning of the GST Act
    `what I do` IS A `What I do`
    @desc The activity you rely on
    `I am carrying it on` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are carrying it on now
    `I am doing something to start it up or wind it up` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are doing something in the course of starting it or ending it
    `I carry it on in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you carry it on in Australia
    `in carrying it on I make supplies connected with the indirect tax zone` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether, in the course or furtherance of carrying it on, you make supplies connected with the indirect tax zone (GST Act s 9-25)

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me and my enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I carry on an enterprise` IF
        (`me`'s `I am carrying it on` OR `me`'s `I am doing something to start it up or wind it up`)
    AND `Is what I do an enterprise` (`me`'s `what I do`) (`me`'s `I am`)
    AND (NOT `Is it my religious institution's activity, not mine` (`me`'s `what I do`))

DECLARE `My ABN entitlement` IS ONE OF
    `not entitled: a limited registration entity is not entitled to an ABN`
    `entitled: a Corporations Act company is entitled to an ABN`
    `not entitled: the activity is treated as my religious institution's, not mine`
    `not entitled: what I do is not an enterprise`
    `not entitled: I am not carrying it on, starting it or winding it up`
    `entitled: I carry on an enterprise in Australia`
    `entitled: I make supplies connected with the indirect tax zone in carrying on my enterprise`
    `not entitled: my enterprise is not in Australia and makes no supplies connected with the indirect tax zone`

@export Am I entitled to an ABN, and why (s 8)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me and my enterprise` @desc Who you are and what you do
GIVETH A `My ABN entitlement`
DECIDE `What is my ABN entitlement` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `me`'s `I am a limited registration entity under the GST Act`
            THEN `not entitled: a limited registration entity is not entitled to an ABN`
        IF `me`'s `I am a company registered under the Corporations Act 2001`
            THEN `entitled: a Corporations Act company is entitled to an ABN`
        IF `Is it my religious institution's activity, not mine` (`me`'s `what I do`)
            THEN `not entitled: the activity is treated as my religious institution's, not mine`
        IF (NOT `Is what I do an enterprise` (`me`'s `what I do`) (`me`'s `I am`))
            THEN `not entitled: what I do is not an enterprise`
        IF (NOT `I carry on an enterprise` `me`)
            THEN `not entitled: I am not carrying it on, starting it or winding it up`
        IF `me`'s `I carry it on in Australia`
            THEN `entitled: I carry on an enterprise in Australia`
        IF `me`'s `in carrying it on I make supplies connected with the indirect tax zone`
            THEN `entitled: I make supplies connected with the indirect tax zone in carrying on my enterprise`
        OTHERWISE `not entitled: my enterprise is not in Australia and makes no supplies connected with the indirect tax zone`

@export Am I entitled to an ABN (s 8)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me and my enterprise` @desc Who you are and what you do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to an ABN` IF
        `What is my ABN entitlement` `me` EQUALS `entitled: a Corporations Act company is entitled to an ABN`
    OR  `What is my ABN entitlement` `me` EQUALS `entitled: I carry on an enterprise in Australia`
    OR  `What is my ABN entitlement` `me` EQUALS `entitled: I make supplies connected with the indirect tax zone in carrying on my enterprise`

§§ `ss 9, 10, 11(2) -- applying for an ABN`

-- s 9(1): "To get an *ABN, *you must apply to the *Registrar to be registered in the *Australian Business Register." Note 1:
-- "You may apply yourself or someone may apply on your behalf." (2): "*Your application must be in the *approved form." (3):
-- "That form may request, but not compel, *you to provide your *TFN or that of an *associate."
-- s 10(1): "The *Registrar must register *you in the *Australian Business Register if: (a) you have applied under section 9;
-- and (b) the Registrar is satisfied that you: (i) are entitled to have an *ABN; or (ii) are likely to be entitled to have
-- an ABN by the date specified in your application; and (c) the Registrar is satisfied that your identity has been
-- established; and (ca) if details about an *associate of yours were requested in the *approved form for registration--the
-- Registrar is satisfied that the identity of the associate has been established; and (d) you are not already registered in
-- the Register."
DECLARE `My ABN application` HAS
    `I applied in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you (or someone for you) applied to the Registrar in the approved form
    `the Registrar is satisfied I am, or by my stated date will likely be, entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied you are entitled to an ABN, or likely to be by the date in your application
    `the Registrar is satisfied of my identity` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied your identity has been established
    `the form asked for details of an associate` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the approved form asked for details about an associate of yours
    `the Registrar is satisfied of the associate's identity` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied the associate's identity has been established
    `I am already registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are already registered in the Australian Business Register

-- s 10 says when the Registrar MUST register; it does not say the Registrar must refuse otherwise. So the other outcomes are
-- phrased "the Registrar need not register me" (and in practice may refuse, s 13).
DECLARE `What happens to my ABN application` IS ONE OF
    `the Registrar must register me and allocate me an ABN`
    `the Registrar need not register me: I have not applied in the approved form`
    `the Registrar need not register me: I am already registered`
    `the Registrar need not register me: not satisfied I am or will be entitled`
    `the Registrar need not register me: not satisfied of my identity`
    `the Registrar need not register me: not satisfied of my associate's identity`

@export Must the Registrar register me and give me an ABN (ss 9, 10)?
GIVEN `my application` IS A `My ABN application` @desc The facts of your application
GIVETH A `What happens to my ABN application`
DECIDE `What happens to my application for an ABN` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `my application`'s `I applied in the approved form`)
            THEN `the Registrar need not register me: I have not applied in the approved form`
        IF `my application`'s `I am already registered`
            THEN `the Registrar need not register me: I am already registered`
        IF (NOT `my application`'s `the Registrar is satisfied I am, or by my stated date will likely be, entitled`)
            THEN `the Registrar need not register me: not satisfied I am or will be entitled`
        IF (NOT `my application`'s `the Registrar is satisfied of my identity`)
            THEN `the Registrar need not register me: not satisfied of my identity`
        IF `my application`'s `the form asked for details of an associate` AND (NOT `my application`'s `the Registrar is satisfied of the associate's identity`)
            THEN `the Registrar need not register me: not satisfied of my associate's identity`
        OTHERWISE `the Registrar must register me and allocate me an ABN`

-- s 9(3): the form "may request, but not compel, *you to provide your *TFN".
@export Must I give my tax file number to get an ABN (s 9(3))?
GIVEN `the form asks for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the approved form asks for your TFN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give my TFN to get an ABN` IF
    `the form asks for it` AND FALSE

-- s 11(2): "The date specified as the date of effect of *your registration may be any date (including a date before your
-- application for registration was made)."
@export Can my ABN registration take effect from a date before I applied (s 11(2))?
GIVEN `the date I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc The date you applied, written YYYYMMDD
      `the date of effect I want` IS A NUMBER @desc The date of effect you ask for, written YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my registration take effect from that date` IF
    `the date of effect I want` < `the date I applied` OR `the date of effect I want` >= `the date I applied`

§§ `s 13(2)-(4) -- may I treat silence as a refusal`

-- s 13(2): "If the *Registrar has not decided *your application for registration under section 9 ... within 28 days after
-- your application is made, you may, at any time, notify the Registrar that you wish to treat your application as having
-- been refused." (3): the Registrar "is taken to have refused your application ... on the day on which the notice is given."
-- (4): "disregard each period (if any): (a) starting on the day on which the *Registrar requests you ... to give the
-- Registrar information; and (b) ending on the day you give the Registrar that information."
-- Days are counted from the application; the 28 days have passed once more than 28 counted days have run (an inference
-- about "within 28 days after").
@export May I treat my ABN application as refused because the Registrar has not decided it (s 13(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `the Registrar has decided it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has decided your application
      `days since I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since your application was made
      `days spent waiting on information the Registrar asked me for` IS A NUMBER @desc Total days from each Registrar request for information to the day you gave it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I treat my application as refused` IF
        (NOT `the Registrar has decided it`)
    AND `days since I applied` - `days spent waiting on information the Registrar asked me for` > 28

§§ `ss 14, 16 -- what I must tell the Registrar`

-- s 14(1): "If: (a) *you give information to the *Registrar; and (b) the information is recorded in relation to you in the
-- *Australian Business Register under section 25; and (c) circumstances change so that the information you gave the
-- Registrar is no longer correct; you must notify the Registrar of the change within 28 days after you become aware of the
-- change." (2): the notice "must be lodged with the *Registrar; and ... must be in the *approved form."
-- s 16(1): "If, but for this subsection, section 14 or 15 would impose an obligation on a *partnership, the obligation is
-- imposed on each partner, but may be discharged by any of the partners." (2): for an unincorporated association or body,
-- "on each member of the committee of management".
-- The Act puts nothing on a company's director or shareholder: a registered company's duty is the company's. (Whether a
-- director answers for the company's breach under the Taxation Administration Act 1953 is not encoded.)
DECLARE `Whose registration it is` IS ONE OF
    `mine`
    `a partnership I am a partner of`
    `an unincorporated association whose committee of management I sit on`
    `a company I direct or own shares in`

@export Is the duty to tell the Registrar of a change mine (ss 14, 16)?
GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Whose registration it is` @desc Whose ABN registration the information is recorded under
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the duty to notify mine` IF
    CONSIDER `the registration`
    WHEN `a company I direct or own shares in` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Must I tell the Registrar about this change (s 14)?
GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Whose registration it is` @desc Whose ABN registration the information is recorded under
      `the information was given to the Registrar and is recorded in the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information was given to the Registrar and recorded against the registration in the Australian Business Register
      `it is no longer correct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether circumstances have changed so that it is no longer correct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the Registrar about the change` IF
        `Is the duty to notify mine` `the registration`
    AND `the information was given to the Registrar and is recorded in the Register`
    AND `it is no longer correct`

@export Am I late telling the Registrar about a change (s 14)?
GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Whose registration it is` @desc Whose ABN registration the information is recorded under
      `the information was given to the Registrar and is recorded in the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information was given to the Registrar and recorded against the registration
      `it is no longer correct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether circumstances have changed so that it is no longer correct
      `days since I became aware of the change` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since you became aware of the change
      `I have lodged the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or, for a partnership or association, any partner or committee member) have lodged the change in the approved form
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I late telling the Registrar` IF
        `Must I tell the Registrar about the change` `the registration` `the information was given to the Registrar and is recorded in the Register` `it is no longer correct`
    AND (NOT `I have lodged the approved form`)
    AND `days since I became aware of the change` > 28

§§ `s 15 -- must I answer the Registrar`

-- s 15(1), item 1: the Registrar may request "*You, if you are registered in the *Australian Business Register" to give
-- "information that is relevant to: (a) your entitlement to be registered; or (b) confirming your identity; or (c) the
-- details entered in relation to you in the Register". "The entity must comply with the request."
-- (2): the request "must specify the period within which the entity is to give the information. The period specified must
-- end at least 14 days after the request is given."
DECLARE `My duty to answer` IS ONE OF
    `I must give the information within the period stated`
    `no duty: I am not registered`
    `no duty: the information is not about my entitlement, my identity or my Register details`
    `no duty yet: the request does not give me the 14 days s 15(2) requires`

@export Must I give the Registrar the information requested, and by when (s 15)?
GIVEN `I am registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered in the Australian Business Register
      `it is about my entitlement, my identity or my Register details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is relevant to your entitlement to be registered, your identity, or your details in the Register
      `days the request gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the request is given the stated period ends
GIVETH A `My duty to answer`
DECIDE `Must I answer the Registrar` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `I am registered`) THEN `no duty: I am not registered`
        IF (NOT `it is about my entitlement, my identity or my Register details`)
            THEN `no duty: the information is not about my entitlement, my identity or my Register details`
        IF `days the request gives me` < 14 THEN `no duty yet: the request does not give me the 14 days s 15(2) requires`
        OTHERWISE `I must give the information within the period stated`

§§ `ss 18, 19 -- when can my ABN be cancelled`

-- s 18(1): "The *Registrar may cancel *your registration in the *Australian Business Register if satisfied that: (a) you are
-- registered under an identity that is not your true identity; or (b) at the time you were registered, you were not
-- entitled to have an *ABN; or (c) you are no longer entitled to have an ABN." Note 1: "If your registration is cancelled,
-- you cease to have an ABN".
-- (4): "The *Registrar may: (a) cancel *your registration if you apply to the Registrar for cancellation of the
-- registration in the *approved form".
-- "May": no ground obliges the Registrar to cancel. Ceasing to carry on an enterprise does not of itself end the ABN.
DECLARE `What could happen to my registration` HAS
    `the Registrar is satisfied I am registered under an identity not my true one` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied you are registered under an identity that is not your true identity
    `the Registrar is satisfied I was not entitled when registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied you were not entitled to an ABN when you were registered
    `the Registrar is satisfied I am no longer entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied you are no longer entitled to an ABN
    `I applied in the approved form to cancel it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you have applied in the approved form to cancel your registration

DECLARE `Can my ABN be cancelled` IS ONE OF
    `yes, the Registrar may cancel it: I am registered under a false identity`
    `yes, the Registrar may cancel it: I was never entitled`
    `yes, the Registrar may cancel it: I am no longer entitled`
    `yes, the Registrar may cancel it at my request`
    `no: there is no ground to cancel it`

@export Can my ABN registration be cancelled, and on what ground (s 18(1), (4))?
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `What could happen to my registration` @desc What the Registrar is satisfied of, and whether you asked
GIVETH A `Can my ABN be cancelled`
DECIDE `Can my ABN registration be cancelled` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the Registrar is satisfied I am registered under an identity not my true one`
            THEN `yes, the Registrar may cancel it: I am registered under a false identity`
        IF `the facts`'s `the Registrar is satisfied I was not entitled when registered`
            THEN `yes, the Registrar may cancel it: I was never entitled`
        IF `the facts`'s `the Registrar is satisfied I am no longer entitled`
            THEN `yes, the Registrar may cancel it: I am no longer entitled`
        IF `the facts`'s `I applied in the approved form to cancel it`
            THEN `yes, the Registrar may cancel it at my request`
        OTHERWISE `no: there is no ground to cancel it`

-- s 18(2): "The *Registrar must notify *you of the cancellation. The notification must state: (a) the reasons for the
-- cancellation; and (b) the date of effect of the cancellation." (3) and (6): the date of effect may be "the date on which
-- *you are given notice ...; a specified date in the future; a date before the date on which the notice is given."
-- (5): on a cancellation at your request, the Registrar must notify you "of the cancellation and the date of effect" (no
-- reasons required).
@export Must I be given reasons when my ABN is cancelled (s 18(2), (5))?
GIVEN `it was cancelled at my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cancellation was on your own application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given reasons for the cancellation` IF
    (NOT `it was cancelled at my request`)

@export Can a cancellation of my ABN take effect from a date before I am told (s 18(3), (6))?
GIVEN `the date I am given notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The date you are given notice, written YYYYMMDD
      `the date of effect stated` IS A NUMBER @desc The date of effect the notice states, written YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the cancellation take effect from that date` IF
        `the date of effect stated` < `the date I am given notice`
    OR  `the date of effect stated` EQUALS `the date I am given notice`
    OR  `the date of effect stated` > `the date I am given notice`

-- s 19(1): "The *Registrar must reinstate *your registration ... if the Registrar is satisfied that the registration should
-- not have been cancelled." (3): "The reinstatement has effect on and from the day on which the registration was
-- cancelled."
@export Must my cancelled ABN be reinstated (s 19)?
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied it should not have been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied the registration should not have been cancelled
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my ABN be reinstated` IF
    `the Registrar is satisfied it should not have been cancelled`

§§ `s 21 -- can I object`

-- s 21(1): "*You may object, in the manner set out in Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953, against a decision
-- you are dissatisfied with that is a *reviewable ABN decision." (2), table: setting the date of effect of your
-- registration (s 11(1)); refusing to register you or your representative (s 13); cancelling your registration (s 18(1));
-- cancelling your representative's registration (s 18(1A)); refusing to cancel your registration or your representative's
-- (s 18(4)); setting the date of effect of a cancellation (s 18(2) or (5)); refusing an application not to disclose details
-- (s 26(4) or 27(7)).
DECLARE `Registrar's decision` IS ONE OF
    `setting the date of effect of my registration`
    `refusing to register me or my representative`
    `cancelling my registration`
    `cancelling my representative's registration`
    `refusing to cancel my registration or my representative's`
    `setting the date of effect of a cancellation`
    `refusing my application not to disclose details`
    `changing my ABN`
    `asking me for information`
    `reinstating my registration`

@export Can I object to this decision of the Registrar (s 21)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Registrar's decision` @desc The Registrar's decision you are dissatisfied with
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I object to the decision` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `changing my ABN` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `asking me for information` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `reinstating my registration` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 23(1) -- using an ABN`

-- s 23(1): "*You must not purport to identify yourself by using: (a) a number that is not an *ABN as if it were an ABN; or
-- (b) an ABN that is not your own. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years."
@export Do I commit an offence by identifying myself with this number as my ABN (s 23(1))?
GIVEN `it is an ABN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the number is an ABN at all (a cancelled registration means you no longer have one)
      `it is my own ABN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ABN is the one allocated to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence by using this number as my ABN` IF
    (NOT `it is an ABN`) OR (NOT `it is my own ABN`)

@export What is the most I can be imprisoned for, in years, for identifying myself with a number that is not my ABN (s 23(1))?
GIVEN `I commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used a number that is not an ABN, or not your ABN, to identify yourself
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Most years of imprisonment for misusing an ABN` IS
    IF `I commit the offence` THEN 2 ELSE 0
